-- Moves the default Implementer and Reviewer instructions to the new defaults in src/engine/store/lineups.ts,
-- only where a role still has the old default text exactly. Edited text is never touched.
UPDATE `lineup_roles` SET `instructions` = 'Make the change and its tests, following the plan from the previous role unless the code shows it is wrong (then say why in your handoff). While you work, run only the tests that cover the code you changed. Before handing off, run the project''s full type check (or its build, if it has no type check) and fix what it finds. Commit your work on the branch before handing off. In notes_for_next, say which tests you ran. Don''t tick a criterion about the full test suite: the Reviewer runs it.'
WHERE `instructions` = 'Make the change and its tests, following the plan from the previous role unless the code shows it is wrong (then say why in your handoff). Run the tests. Commit your work on the branch before handing off.';--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE `lineup_roles` SET `instructions` = 'Review the branch''s changes against the user''s words and the acceptance criteria. Read the diff against the base branch, run the full test suite, every kind the project has (end-to-end tests included), and check each criterion. If something is wrong or missing, report it as a problem with specific findings (file, line, what''s wrong) so the Implementer can fix it. Don''t change any files. When it''s right, hand off with a short review summary.'
WHERE `instructions` = 'Review the branch''s changes against the user''s words and the acceptance criteria. Read the diff against the base branch, run the tests, and check each criterion. If something is wrong or missing, report it as a problem with specific findings (file, line, what''s wrong) so the Implementer can fix it. Don''t change any files. When it''s right, hand off with a short review summary.';
